# Bilbo, Luckwearer's Adventure, Burglar's Plot (CR 715): "Exchange control of two target nonland permanents that share a card type"
# (CR 701.12a, 205.2a). Bot1 holds Ornithopter (an artifact creature) and five Moxen; Bot2 has Grizzly Bears and a Forest. Bot1 casts it on
# turn 3 for {4}{U} with the five Moxen (the pool empty after). The refusals: Mox Sapphire and Grizzly Bears share no card type (an artifact and a
# creature), Forest is a land, and one target or three (three Moxen share the artifact type) are the wrong number. Ornithopter and Grizzly Bears share the creature type: the exchange happens, Ornithopter is Bot2's and Grizzly
# Bears Bot1's (summoning sick). The card is exiled, not in the graveyard, so Bilbo can later be cast from it.

